## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable cross-tenant feature store with strict data isolation, dynamic versioning, drift/compliance checks, and robust rollback in OTCA contexts.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant data isolation and versioned schemas
- Region-specific streaming with Kafka
- Parquet/ORC storage with tenant/date partitions
- Drift detection and compliance auditing
- Canary deployments for schema evolution

## Code Example
```javascript
// Implementation sketch
type FeatureRecord = {
  tenant_id: string;
  feature_id: string;
  version: string;
  region: string;
  event_type: 'feature_request'|'feature_update'|'drift_alert'|'compliance_violation';
  timestamp: string;
  payload_hash: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement rollback across tenants without data loss?
- How do you enforce per-tenant residency in cross-region reads?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design a schema-evolution friendly path in an OTCA pipeline, a critical, often overlooked area for long-lived telemetry.

## Key Concepts
- Schema Registry
- Versioning and migrations
- Per-tenant isolation
- Data fidelity and compatibility

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo mapping
function mapEvent(event, registry) {
  const latest = registry.latestFor(event.type);
  const v = event.schema_version ?? 1;
  if (v < latest.version) {
    return migrate(event, v, latest.version);
  }
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle breaking changes across tenants?
- How would you test migrations at scale?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?
